p276.setupPrompt:
Please use the agentj-workflow-wizard skill (the Workflow Design Bible method) to set up my organization:
1. Look at the folders one level under the working root and find the projects I actually use;
2. For those already organized this way (an entry file and the documentation/ boot documents), only review them; fill gaps with `agentj wizard apply`, never over files I changed;
3. For projects in use but not organized yet, list them for me first and complete their documents with the wizard only after I agree; do not move, delete or edit the projects' own work files;
4. Register every workflow's CEO in the CEO roster documentation/ROLES.md: run `agentj wizard register --dir . --json`, then check with `agentj wizard doctor --dir . --json`;
5. For each company with only a CEO and no staff yet (its card says so), read its latest reports/, task.json and the roles in RUN.md, propose 3–7 staff roles (name, what each does, when to send it) and list them for me first; only after I agree, write them with `agentj wizard apply` to `<folder>/.claude/agents/<role>.md` (the Codex `.codex/agents/<role>.toml` is made with it), never over files I changed;
6. Finally tell me what you registered, what you added, what is still missing, and which cards the phone's Workflows page will show.

p276.reviewPrompt:
Please use the agentj-workflow-wizard skill (the Workflow Design Bible method) to review my organization. This is a review, not a redo:
1. Look at the folders one level under the working root against the CEO roster documentation/ROLES.md and find new projects that are not registered;
2. For organized ones, only review the entry file and the documentation/ boot documents; fill gaps with `agentj wizard apply`, never over files I changed;
3. List new, unorganized projects for me first and complete them with the wizard only after I agree; do not move, delete or edit the projects' own work files;
4. Run `agentj wizard register --dir . --json` to fill the roster, then check with `agentj wizard doctor --dir . --json`;
5. For each company with only a CEO and no staff yet (its card says so), read its latest reports/, task.json and the roles in RUN.md, propose 3–7 staff roles (name, what each does, when to send it) and list them for me first; only after I agree, write them with `agentj wizard apply` to `<folder>/.claude/agents/<role>.md` (the Codex `.codex/agents/<role>.toml` is made with it), never over files I changed;
6. Tell me only what this review found and fixed, what is still missing, and which cards the phone's Workflows page will show.
